description:
The site names only the repository. Add an About page, linked from every page, that says:
- who makes the site (an independent AI engineering consultancy) and that it is self-funded;
- for each engine, what it is, who makes it, which version or checkpoint was tested, and how it was accessed. For the hosted engine: paid API access only, no other relationship with its maker. For the open-source engines: package or repository, checkpoint hash, hardware and precision;
- how to contact the authors and report an error in a result;
- that the site uses analytics, with the opt-out.
Keep it factual and short; it is a disclosure, not a pitch.
